   "answer": "Sorry you're seeing that \u2014 here are the specific steps that usually fix pages not appearing on the live site. Please try them and tell me the result. 1) Confirm publish and preview: In the editor click Publish, then View Site (or Preview) to confirm the change is on the live site. (The KB notes publishing is required for changes to appear live) [1]. 2) Clear local issues: Clear your browser cache and make sure your browser is supported or up to date, or run the Wix Technical Assistant to check for local problems [1]. 3) Check page visibility and menu settings: Make sure the page isn't hidden and that you have a menu added to the site \u2014 \"Your Wix site's menu automatically displays every page added to your site except for pages you've chosen to hide\" [5]. If the menu is missing on the live site, follow the Menu > Pages > Settings > Layouts steps and set the page to Standard, then Publish again [5]. 4) Check header/footer and overlapping items: If the menu or page link doesn\u2019t respond, confirm the header/footer aren\u2019t hidden or frozen and that nothing is overlapping the menu (bring the menu to the front) as detailed in the Menu Issues article, then Publish and refresh the live site [5]. 5) Check site history and collaborators: If edits were overwritten, open Site History to find and restore the last saved version that has the pages, and verify whether a collaborator saved over changes [1]. 6) Disable custom code if present: Custom code can cause unexpected results; follow the Disable Custom Code steps in the Wix Technical Assistant if you suspect code is affecting the live site [1]. If you try these and the pages still don\u2019t appear, tell me (a) whether the pages are visible in the editor and in Preview, (b) whether they appear in Menus & Pages and are set to show, and (c) whether you have custom code or collaborators on the site \u2014 I\u2019ll use that info to guide the next step. [1][5]",
