   "reasoning": "The customer wants the stray logo removed from their live (published) site when it does not appear in the editor. The KB contains troubleshooting steps for differences between the editor and the live site that are directly relevant: for example, \u201cClick Publish in your editor, then check your live site to see if it has updated.\u201d [2] and \u201cCustom code can have unexpected results that affect your site's performance. Follow the Disable Custom Code steps in the Wix Technical Assistant to resolve the issue.\u201d [2]. However, the correct troubleshooting path depends on details you haven't provided (which page has the stray logo, whether you've published since editing, whether collaborators may have overwritten changes, whether custom code or browser caching is involved). Asking for those specifics will determine which KB procedure to use (publish, restore from site history, disable custom code, clear cache, check collaborators). No human action is required at this point because the KB procedures cover the possible causes and fixes.",
   "answer": "Please provide the following so I can walk you through the right steps: 1) The Wix site name or URL and which page shows the stray logo (or a public page URL). 2) Have you made changes in the editor and clicked Publish since then? 3) Are there other site collaborators who might have saved changes? 4) Do you have any custom code added to the site? 5) Which browser and device are you using, and have you tried clearing your browser cache or testing in a different supported browser? 6) Please attach a screenshot of the live page showing the stray logo (and, if possible, a screenshot of the editor page where the logo does not appear). With these details I can follow the relevant KB steps (publish check, site history restore, disable custom code, or browser/cache troubleshooting) to resolve the issue. [2]",
   "v4_decision": "CLARIFY",
   "reference_answer": "If you are unable to select or find an element in the editor, it is possible that it has been placed behind another element. Follow the steps below to locate and select your elements in the editor.\n\n## Use the Layers panel to locate an element\nIf an element is placed outside the editor gridlines or behind another element, you may not be able to see it on your screen. Use the Layers panel to locate the element on the page.\n## To open the Layers panel and find elements:\n1. [Go to your editor](https://manage.wix.com/account/site-selector/?actionUrl=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.wix.com%2Feditor%2F%7BmetaSiteId%7D%3FeditorSessionId%3D%7Besi%7D%26).\n2. Click the **Layers** icon ![](https://lh6.googleusercontent.com/gK9dfcU80SWT9YOMhPhN62hW4YUDMmaf17w7O0LfSHLFn46W1Nugy_36zibPxclwtc5OmziXxiJ-zGwzz956EAjx8MqPYVd_i7KRCOZU9Sq7-7KUE-tjh3C5Lhgyto4oz9h2J5E5-59p__W4gjiJwg) at the bottom of your editor.\n3. Click **Header**, **Page** or **Footer**.\n4. Find the relevant element on the list and click to select it.\n\n## Use Ctrl + Shift + M to toggle through your elements\nIf you see an element on your live site or in Preview mode, but not in the editor, it might be placed outside of the site's gridlines. Toggle through your page elements to locate the element.\nTo toggle through elements on a page:\n1. Hold down Ctrl (Cmd on Mac) + Shift on your keyboard.\n2. Press M to scroll through the elements on your site until you reach the desired element.\n",
