   "reasoning": "The customer wants help because a 50% off coupon in Wix Stores is not applying. The KB includes how to create coupons and several relevant notes (e.g., creating % coupons and where to set Apply to, minimum subtotal, and that promo codes must be visible on the cart page) [1][4]. However, the ticket doesn't give the specific details that determine which KB procedure or note applies (coupon code, coupon settings, cart subtotal, product type, payment method, whether this is a subscription, expiration or usage limits, or any error messages). Asking for those specifics would change the next steps (TEST A and TEST B): the appropriate troubleshooting steps depend on settings the customer can supply, and the excerpts contain the procedures and checks to perform [1][4]. A human is not required at this stage. Therefore we should CLARIFY and request the precise details needed to apply the documented procedures.",
   "answer": "I can help troubleshoot \u2014 please provide the following so I can apply the correct KB steps: 1) Your site name or URL and the coupon code you\u2019re trying to use. 2) Is this for a subscription (recurring plan) or a one-time product/order? Note: coupons applied to subscriptions behave differently ([2],[4]). 3) How did you create the coupon (percent vs $ discount) and what did you set in the Apply to field (All products, Specific category, Minimum order subtotal)? The KB shows % coupons and the Apply to options for Wix Stores [1][4]. 4) What is the cart subtotal at checkout (in case a minimum order subtotal was set)? The KB requires the subtotal to meet the minimum for the coupon to work [4]. 5) Is the promo code field visible on your cart page? The KB notes the promo code field must be visible to redeem coupons [4]. 6) Which payment method did you select at checkout (e.g., Manual payment)? The KB notes behavior differs for manual payments [4]. 7) Does the coupon have start/end dates, usage limits, or a limit to one use per customer? 8) Are you seeing any error messages or behavior (for example: coupon appears but no discount, or code is rejected)? Please include a screenshot if possible. With those details I\u2019ll follow the relevant KB steps to identify why the 50% coupon isn\u2019t applying [1][4].",
   "v4_decision": "CLARIFY",
   "reference_answer": "Check If the Coupon is Out-of-Date:\nWhen creating a coupon, you can limit when it can be used. For example, a \"June Sale\" coupon might be active from June 1 to June 30. Customers trying to use it outside these dates will be unable to apply the coupon.\nEdit the dates to extend the validity if necessary.\n\nCheck the Visibility of the Promo Code Link:\nEnsure the \"Enter a promo code\" link is enabled.\nVerify that the font color of the link contrasts with your site's background color so it is visible.\n\nEnsure the Coupon is Activated:\nIf a coupon is deactivated, customers will not be able to use it.\nReactivate the coupon in your settings if needed.\n\nCheck If the Coupon Reached Its Usage Limit:\nCoupons can be limited by total usage or to one use per person. For example, the first 50 people to use a discount.\nIf the coupon has exceeded its usage limits, it won't be applicable for more customers.\n\nVerify the Coupon Code Format:\nCustomers may mistakenly add spaces to the coupon code (e.g., \"March Madness\" instead of \"MarchMadness\"), rendering it invalid.\nAdvise customers to copy and paste the coupon code carefully without any additional spaces.",
