   "answer": "Try these steps to select the overlapping Google Maps element and remove it from the footer:\n\n1) Select the overlapping element using the right-click Overlapping Items menu: In the Editor, right-click an element near the map, hover over \"Overlapping Items,\" and click the Google Maps element from the list to select it. \"Right-click an element in the editor. Hover over Overlapping Items. Click the relevant element from the list.\" [2]\n\n2) If you prefer the Layers panel: open Layers (bottom-left of the editor), choose Header, Page or Footer, then find and click the Google Maps element to select it. [1][2]\n\n3) You can also toggle through page elements: hold Ctrl (Cmd on Mac) + Shift and press M to cycle forward (Ctrl/Cmd + M to go backward) until you reach the map. [1][2]\n\n4) If the footer is covering the map, check whether the footer is frozen: click the footer, click the Settings icon, and check the Freeze Footer toggle. If it\u2019s enabled, disable it or resize the footer so it doesn\u2019t overlap your map. \"Click the footer in your Editor. Click the Settings icon. Check the Freeze Footer toggle\" [3]\n\n5) To remove the map from the footer so it no longer appears on all pages: drag and drop the map away from the footer and into another area of the page (drop it when the editor shows the page area). \"Just drag and drop the element away from the header or footer and into another area of your page.\" [5]\n\nIf you try these steps and still can\u2019t select or remove the map, tell me what happens at which step (for example: you don\u2019t see \"Overlapping Items\" in the right-click menu, or the map won\u2019t drag out of the footer) and I\u2019ll provide the next troubleshooting steps.",
